                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is a good example of why an arbitrary yes or no review system doesn't really work for a game. It was a tough decision and I flip flopped back and forth as it is not a horrible game but given the current price tag of $22CAD, I cannot recommend this game. \n\nFirst off about the game. The simplest way for me to describe The Bradwell Conspiracy is sort of like Firewatch meets Portal, but it is sadly not as good as either. It is essentially a linear walking-sim with some very light puzzle solving in which you are trying to escape a collapsed building and find out how you got there. Like in Firewatch you have someone on the other end of the comm system throughout the game giving you tips and feeding you story. You also have the ability to take a picture of anything and it will send it to this person. I feel like this was kind of a missed opportunity as there could be more puzzles using this feature, but as it stands it is mainly just used if you get stuck or to progress the story and open a door. \n\nThe other major gameplay hook is that you have a sort of 3D printer gun that lets you store and print a few different items to help you progress through the levels. I feel like this is the biggest let down for me as it is a great concept however you really only use it to get across gaps and I feel like the \"puzzles\" if you can call them that, are few and far between. It is also extremely finicky and frustrating. It often doesnt let you build something where you want to, which after a lot of trial and error, turns out to be exactly where you are supposed to build it..\n\n[b]The Good[/b]\n[list]\n[*]The story/ setting was interesting and kept me intrigued until the end.\n[*]The voice acting is great.\n[*]The visual style is nice and works well for the game, although it doesn't always look the greatest even on Ultra.\n[/list]\n[b]The Okay[/b]\n[list]\n[*]In theory the gameplay concepts such as the 3D Printer gun and camera are good, I just wish they were used better and more frequently.\n[/list]\n[b]The Bad[/b]\n[list]\n[*]The use of the 3D printer gun in game. As the 3D printer is pretty well the only game play mechanic outside of walking, it runs in to a lot of problems. For example, you will have to print platforms at various points to get across a gap in walkway. Now there is no puzzle as you know you have to get across and you have the ability to build platforms so you should just be able to make the platform and continue. However, the game will just not let you build the platform anywhere! You will spend 10 minutes trying to find the perfect exact spot the game will let you build the platform (I am talking in game inches not feet) and then just shake your head and move on.\n[*]Length.  I think you are looking at 3 hours, maximum 4 hours if you 100% the game and read the few emails and posters on the wall for additional story tidbits. (I am not sure what my game time will say as i went out for dinner midway through my play through and didnt shut it off) I think the game could have used a couple more hours to build up the story and have a few more puzzles as it does go by very quickly and for the price this would be a deal breaker for me.\n[/list]\n\nOverall I think the game is worth checking out for the interesting style/story, but given its length, current price and occasional frustration I would recommend waiting for a decent sale.",
